cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its result packages, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Lunar Site Navigator"
abstract: >-
  Lunar Site Navigator computes, for any point on the Moon, the 360-degree terrain
  horizon from NASA LOLA elevation data and the directions of the Sun and the Earth with
  NASA SPICE, and reports when each is visible, which terrain blocks it and how many hours
  that costs. Results are published as versioned packages with SHA-256 checksums, read by
  a web viewer and an Unreal Engine planner, and compared with independent sources on a
  validation card. Made by team Kestro Aerospace for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026,
  challenge "Lunar Landing Site Navigator".
